import Mathlib
import TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.AbelianVariety.Isogeny

/-!
# Abelian schemes and arithmetic moduli, part II: target signatures

The roadmap is README.md; this file is not the roadmap. It states the roadmap's
headline theorems against the pinned Mathlib and Tau Ceti APIs.

The statable headlines are resultant recognition (F2.2), the fixed-field
isogeny-class asymptotic (F6.5), and the coarse prime-field isomorphism-class
bound (F6.4). The last two use actual abelian varieties and quotients by
isogenies and isomorphisms, including inseparable isogenies. Their finiteness
conjuncts (finitely many isogeny classes, finitely many isomorphism classes in
each dimension over a finite field) are theorems of ArithmeticStatisticsPartI
(§0.16 and its supporting constructions, which also own the Weil-polynomial
bound and Tate's theorem at every prime); they are stated here only because the
growth assertions are about their cardinalities.

The other headlines are not statable at the pins:
* P0.5's shuffle-compatible divided-power comparison needs the all-degree
  shuffle algebra; native tensor powers and the divided-power algebra alone
  do not supply that algebra structure.
* P2.8's completed Poincaré cohomology, P3.3–P3.4's logarithm and smooth
  comparisons, and P4.2–P4.3's ordinary CM trivialization and connection
  compatibility need relative abelian schemes, their universal vector
  extensions, completed Poincaré coefficient sheaves and connection carriers.
* B1.4's Betti-form rank criterion, B2.3–B2.4's bounded-degree torsion
  and fixed-part theorems, B2.21–B2.23's specialness and full-rank theorems,
  B3's mixed Ax–Schanuel, closed degeneracy loci and quotient criterion,
  and B4's fibre-power and curve-difference non-degeneracy need relative
  abelian-family analytification and Betti maps, trace and Hodge-variation
  carriers, mixed Kuga uniformizations and fine curve moduli, respectively.
* F3.2's Honda–Tate correspondence, F3.4–F3.5/F3.7–F3.8/F3.10's
  prime-field linear-dual comparisons and order realization, and F4.8's
  fixed-level isomorphism bound need the abelian
  Frobenius characteristic polynomial, the Galois-equivariant Tate functor on
  abelian varieties, the contravariant Dieudonné realization, rational
  markings and all-prime realization lattice spaces.
* F5.7–F5.9's CM Hermitian mass and polarization growth and bounds, and
  F6.6's squarefree nonreal ppav proportion need integral Hermitian lattice
  and polarization carriers with their orbit dictionaries. The finite-n
  ordinary-isogeny lower bound in F6.5 additionally needs the ordinary
  abelian-variety predicate.

The general trace and Lang–Néron theorem are inputs from
HeightsRationalPointsAndObstructions §§1.9–1.10; uniform torsion closures in families
are inputs from its §5.8. The general marked all-prime
lattice correspondence and rational-orbit quotient are inputs from
ArithmeticStatisticsPartI's supporting construction "Finiteness of an isogeny
class and of unpolarized classes"; only their prime-field linear-dual adapters
are new headlines here.

No auxiliary theorem or weakened substitute represents a missing headline.
-/

noncomputable section

namespace TauCetiRoadmap.AbelianSchemesAndArithmeticModuliPartII

open CategoryTheory
open scoped BigOperators

universe u

/-! ## Layer F2: Resultant recognition -/

/-- Monic tests from a uniformizer-adically dense subring determine a monic DVR polynomial. -/
theorem resultantRecognition {D O : Type*} [CommRing D] [CommRing O] [IsDomain O]
    [IsDiscreteValuationRing O] (φ : D →+* O) (π : O) (hπ : Irreducible π)
    (hφ : ∀ N : ℕ, ∀ o : O, ∃ d : D, o - φ d ∈ Ideal.span {π ^ N})
    (P Q : Polynomial O) (hP : P.Monic) (hQ : Q.Monic)
    (h : ∀ ψ : Polynomial D, ψ.Monic →
      Polynomial.resultant P (ψ.map φ) ≠ 0 →
      Polynomial.resultant Q (ψ.map φ) ≠ 0 →
      IsDiscreteValuationRing.addVal O (Polynomial.resultant P (ψ.map φ)) =
        IsDiscreteValuationRing.addVal O (Polynomial.resultant Q (ψ.map φ))) :
    P = Q := by
  sorry

/-! ## Layer F6: Counting isogeny and isomorphism classes -/

/-- Abelian varieties over k of dimension g, on the pinned geometric carrier. -/
abbrev AbelianVarietiesOfDimension (k : Type u) [Field k] (g : ℕ) :=
  {A : TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.AbelianVariety k // A.dim = (g : WithBot ℕ∞)}

/-- Dimension-g abelian varieties modulo the equivalence relation generated by k-isogenies.
The native isogeny predicate means finite and surjective, without separability. -/
def AbelianIsogenyClasses (k : Type u) [Field k] (g : ℕ) :=
  Quot (fun A B : AbelianVarietiesOfDimension k g =>
    ∃ f : A.val ⟶ B.val, TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.AbelianVariety.IsIsogeny f)

/-- Dimension-g abelian varieties modulo k-isomorphism, without a polarization or a marking. -/
def AbelianIsomorphismClasses (k : Type u) [Field k] (g : ℕ) :=
  Quot (fun A B : AbelianVarietiesOfDimension k g => Nonempty (A.val ≅ B.val))

/-- Over a fixed finite field of cardinality q, the logarithm of the number of
isogeny classes, divided by g², tends to (log q)/4. Finiteness is part of the assertion;
it is ArithmeticStatisticsPartI's Weil-polynomial finiteness with its isogeny criterion.
DiPippo–Howe, Theorem 1.3; Lipnowski–Tsimerman, Corollary 2.2. -/
theorem isogenyClassAsymptotic (k : Type u) [Field k] [Finite k] :
    (∀ g : ℕ, Finite (AbelianIsogenyClasses k g)) ∧
      Filter.Tendsto
        (fun g : ℕ => Real.log (Nat.card (AbelianIsogenyClasses k g) : ℝ) / (g : ℝ) ^ 2)
        Filter.atTop (nhds (Real.log (Nat.card k : ℝ) / 4)) := by
  sorry

/-- For a fixed prime p, dimension-g abelian varieties over F_p have finitely many
isomorphism classes (ArithmeticStatisticsPartI §0.16) and their logarithmic count is
O_p(g²). Lee, Theorem 1.1; only the coarse bound specified in F6.4 is asserted. -/
theorem isomorphismClassCount (p : ℕ) [Fact p.Prime] :
    (∀ g : ℕ, Finite (AbelianIsomorphismClasses (ZMod p) g)) ∧
      Asymptotics.IsBigO Filter.atTop
        (fun g : ℕ => Real.log (Nat.card (AbelianIsomorphismClasses (ZMod p) g) : ℝ))
        (fun g : ℕ => (g : ℝ) ^ 2) := by
  sorry

end TauCetiRoadmap.AbelianSchemesAndArithmeticModuliPartII
